IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa18-part22-interest`
IMPORT `coa18-part22-notice`

-- coa18-tests-part22-notice.l4: tests for coa18-part22-notice.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 791 to 807).
-- Every expected value is written from the text, beside its assertion, before the run; a failing assertion is a finding.
-- Generated by work/gentests.py from work/tests/part22-notice.py (the layout only; the values are hand-written).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: see the header of coa18-part22-notice.l4.
-- Fixtures and directives are named with the section label so that no name collides with another part.

§§ `the last day of each period of working days (s 827 stepper)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` MEANS
    (NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (elem d (LIST (Date 6 1 2026))))

-- 805(1): 15 working days after Thursday 1 January 2026, skipping weekends and the listed Tuesday 6 January: Friday 23 January
#ASSERT `s 805(1) the last day for making the report available for inspection` (Date 1 1 2026) `s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` EQUALS (Date 23 1 2026)
-- 805(1): 15 working days after Monday 5 January, counted by weeks: 3 in the week of 5 January (the listed Tuesday 6 is skipped), 5 and 5 in the next two weeks (13), then Monday 26 (14) and Tuesday 27 January (15). First written as 26 January in error (a slip in the hand count, found by this assertion; the calendar count above gives 27)
#ASSERT `s 805(1) the last day for making the report available for inspection` (Date 5 1 2026) `s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` EQUALS (Date 27 1 2026)
-- 805(3): 15 working days after Tuesday 31 March 2026: Tuesday 21 April
#ASSERT `s 805(3) the last day for making the report available for inspection` (Date 31 3 2026) `s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` EQUALS (Date 21 4 2026)
-- 805(6): 3 working days after Friday 2 January: Monday 5, Wednesday 7 (6 January listed), Thursday 8
#ASSERT `s 805(6) the last day for notifying the members who made the requests` (Date 2 1 2026) `s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` EQUALS (Date 8 1 2026)
-- 807(2): 10 working days after Monday 5 January: Tuesday 20 January
#ASSERT `s 807(2) the last day for providing the copy` (Date 5 1 2026) `s 805 test: a day is a working day unless it is a weekend or 6 January 2026` EQUALS (Date 20 1 2026)

§§ `s 791 and s 792`

-- a public company: the Part applies (s 791 "only" read as closing; fork F1)
#ASSERT `s 791 this Part applies to the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a private company: "This Part applies only to public companies."
#ASSERT `s 791 this Part applies to the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- issued shares of a class carrying votes in all circumstances
#ASSERT `s 792(1) the shares are the company's shares for the purposes of this Part` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- treasury shares are included: "(including any shares held as treasury shares)"
#ASSERT `s 792(1) the shares are the company's shares for the purposes of this Part` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- issued shares of a class that does not carry votes in all circumstances are not "the company's shares" for the Part
#ASSERT `s 792(1) the shares are the company's shares for the purposes of this Part` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- shares neither issued nor held as treasury shares
#ASSERT `s 792(1) the shares are the company's shares for the purposes of this Part` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a temporary suspension "does not affect the application of this Part"
#ASSERT `s 792(2) a suspension of voting rights affects the application of this Part to interests in those or any other shares` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a suspension that is not temporary: not covered
#ASSERT `s 792(2) a suspension of voting rights affects the application of this Part to interests in those or any other shares` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 793 notice requiring information`

-- (a): the company believes the person is interested
#ASSERT `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): the company believes the person was interested in the last three years
#ASSERT `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no knowledge or belief: the grant names whom; not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- first day of the three years (15 June 2023)
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 15 6 2023) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before the window opens
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 14 6 2023) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day immediately preceding the notice
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 14 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the notice date itself does not "precede" it (a present interest is limb (a); fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- leap day notice: three years back is 28 February 2021 (clamped), inclusive
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 28 2 2021) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one day before the clamped start
#ASSERT `s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` (Date 27 2 2021) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a): a notice the company may give may require confirmation
#ASSERT `s 793(2)(a) the notice may require the person to confirm that fact or to state whether or not it is the case` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2)(a): the company may not give a notice: not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(2)(a) the notice may require the person to confirm that fact or to state whether or not it is the case` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a): the company's power under (1) is not known: not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(2)(a) the notice may require the person to confirm that fact or to state whether or not it is the case` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b): "if he holds, or has during that time held, any such interest"
#ASSERT `s 793(2)(b) the notice may require the person to give further information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 793(2)(b) the notice may require the person to give further information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; a function named for a power or grant (the notice may require) answered JUST FALSE because an if gate failed; the name-test sweep makes it NOTHING, since the text limits the grant in its own wording and does not say the power is lacking outside the gate (fork F42); facts unchanged
-- (2)(b): no such interest
#ASSERT `s 793(2)(b) the notice may require the person to give further information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): an interest held during the three years
#ASSERT `s 793(3) the notice may require the person to give particulars of his own present or past interest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): an interest not within the three year period: not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(3) the notice may require the person to give particulars of his own present or past interest` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)(a): present interest and another subsists
#ASSERT `s 793(4) the notice may require the person to give such particulars with respect to that other interest as the notice requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4)(b): another subsisted while his interest subsisted
#ASSERT `s 793(4) the notice may require the person to give such particulars with respect to that other interest as the notice requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4): "where" neither (a) nor (b)
#ASSERT `s 793(4) the notice may require the person to give such particulars with respect to that other interest as the notice requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5)(a): identity of persons interested
#ASSERT `s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` TRUE `s 793(5)(a) the identity of persons interested in the shares in question` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5)(b)(i): agreement to which section 824 applies
#ASSERT `s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` TRUE `s 793(5)(b)(i) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement to which section 824 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5)(b)(ii): agreement or arrangement relating to the exercise of rights
#ASSERT `s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` TRUE `s 793(5)(b)(ii) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement or arrangement relating to the exercise of any rights conferred by the holding of the shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5): "include" does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` TRUE `s 793(5) another kind of particular` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): particulars not asked under (3) or (4): not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` FALSE `s 793(5)(a) the identity of persons interested in the shares in question` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): a past interest
#ASSERT `s 793(6) the notice may require the person to give particulars of the identity of the person who held that interest immediately upon his ceasing to hold it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (6): "where his interest is a past interest"
#ASSERT `s 793(6) the notice may require the person to give particulars of the identity of the person who held that interest immediately upon his ceasing to hold it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7): given on the last day specified
#ASSERT `s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` TRUE (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 10 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (7): given before the last day
#ASSERT `s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` TRUE (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (7): given the day after the time specified
#ASSERT `s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` TRUE (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 11 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7): the time specified is not reasonable: the text says "such reasonable time": not covered
#ASSERT `s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` FALSE (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 794 order imposing restrictions`

-- (1): notice served on a person who is or was interested, and he has failed to give the information in time
#ASSERT `s 794(1) the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1): the person did give the information: "Where ... (b)" fails
#ASSERT `s 794(1) the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): no notice under section 793 was served on him
#ASSERT `s 794(1) the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the court is satisfied that third parties' rights may be unfairly affected
#ASSERT `s 794(2) the court may direct that acts set out in the order shall not constitute a breach of the restrictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 794(2) the court may direct that acts set out in the order shall not constitute a breach of the restrictions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; a function named for a power or grant (the court may direct) answered JUST FALSE because an if gate failed; the name-test sweep makes it NOTHING, since the text limits the grant in its own wording and does not say the power is lacking outside the gate (fork F43); facts unchanged
-- (2): "If the court is satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 794(2) the court may direct that acts set out in the order shall not constitute a breach of the restrictions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): on an application under the section
#ASSERT `s 794(3) the court may make an interim order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): no application ("on" read as "where")
#ASSERT `s 794(3) the court may make an interim order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): unconditionally
#ASSERT `s 794(3) the interim order may be made in this way` `s 794(3) unconditionally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): on such terms as the court thinks fit
#ASSERT `s 794(3) the interim order may be made in this way` `s 794(3) on such terms as the court thinks fit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): a third way is not mentioned
#ASSERT `s 794(3) the interim order may be made in this way` `s 794(3) in another way` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 795 offences and penalty`

-- (1)(a): fails to comply, no defence proved
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(a) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): "does not commit an offence ... if he proves that the requirement ... was frivolous or vexatious"
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(a) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(a): he complied: a person who complied is not mentioned
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(a) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b)(i): knowingly false
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(b)(ii): recklessly false
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(b): a statement neither known to be false nor recklessly false: not covered
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b): no statement in purported compliance: not covered
#ASSERT `s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a): imprisonment not exceeding two years or a fine (or both)
#ASSERT `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `on conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
-- (3)(b)(i): twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both)
#ASSERT `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `on summary conviction in England and Wales` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
-- (3)(b)(ii): six months, Scotland
#ASSERT `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `on summary conviction in Scotland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
-- (3)(b)(ii): six months, Northern Ireland
#ASSERT `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
-- (3)(b): summary conviction is divided by place; without a place: not covered
#ASSERT `s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` `on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 796 exemption`

-- (1): exempted by the Secretary of State
#ASSERT `s 796(1) the person is not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1): not exempted: this section does not say he is obliged; not covered
#ASSERT `s 796(1) the person is not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): both conditions met, so the bar does not apply ("unless")
#ASSERT `s 796(2) the Secretary of State is barred from granting the exemption` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): not satisfied: "must not grant"
#ASSERT `s 796(2) the Secretary of State is barred from granting the exemption` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): the Governor of the Bank of England was not consulted
#ASSERT `s 796(2) the Secretary of State is barred from granting the exemption` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): neither
#ASSERT `s 796(2) the Secretary of State is barred from granting the exemption` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 797 consequences of an order`

-- (1)(a): shares under an order, no direction
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(a): no order: the effect of an order is not stated for other shares
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)(a): within a direction under s 794(2) or s 799(3): "subject to" (fork F4)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(b): permitted by the terms of an interim order
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(b): no order
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b) subject to (4)(a)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(c)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(c) no further shares may be issued in right of the shares or in pursuance of an offer made to their holder` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(c) subject to (4)(b)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(c) no further shares may be issued in right of the shares or in pursuance of an offer made to their holder` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(d): payment outside a liquidation
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(d): "except in a liquidation"
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(d): no order
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(d) subject to (4)(a)
#ASSERT `s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): shares under the (1)(a) restriction
#ASSERT `s 797(2) an agreement to transfer the shares is void` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2): "Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(a)" fails
#ASSERT `s 797(2) an agreement to transfer the shares is void` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): "This does not apply to an agreement to transfer the shares on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)"
#ASSERT `s 797(2) an agreement to transfer the shares is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) subject to (4)(a)
#ASSERT `s 797(2) an agreement to transfer the shares is void` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): shares under (1)(c) or (d) and a right to be issued shares or to receive a payment
#ASSERT `s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): "Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(c) or (d)" fails
#ASSERT `s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): an agreement about something other than those rights: not mentioned
#ASSERT `s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the court-approved transfer exception
#ASSERT `s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) subject to (4)(b)
#ASSERT `s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(a): a direction
#ASSERT `s 797(4) the provisions of section 797 are displaced for the act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4)(b): the terms of an interim order
#ASSERT `s 797(4) the provisions of section 797 are displaced for the act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (4): neither: not mentioned
#ASSERT `s 797(4) the provisions of section 797 are displaced for the act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 798 evasion of restrictions`

-- (1): shares subject to restrictions by virtue of an order under section 794
#ASSERT `s 798(1) this section applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1): "This section applies where ..."
#ASSERT `s 798(1) this section applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a)(i): disposes of shares known to be restricted
