§§ `the duties as regulative rules (#TRACE; check.sh counts no assertion for these, so the expected outcome is in the comment)`

-- 796(2) as a regulative rule: when both conditions are met the rule reduces to FULFILLED, which an assertion can compare (a standing prohibition cannot be compared with EQUALS on this binary: see NOTES.md)
#ASSERT `s 796(2) the Secretary of State must not grant the exemption unless the conditions are met` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED

-- expected: FULFILLED (given on day 5 of 10)
#TRACE `s 793(7) the person addressed must give the information required by the notice` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 793(7) the person to whom the notice is addressed` DOES `s 793(7) give the information required by the notice` AT 5

-- expected: DEONTIC BREACHED (given on day 11 of 10)
#TRACE `s 793(7) the person addressed must give the information required by the notice` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 793(7) the person to whom the notice is addressed` DOES `s 793(7) give the information required by the notice` AT 11

-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 804(1) the company that is required under section 803 must exercise its powers in the manner specified` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 804(1) exercises its powers under section 793 in the manner specified in the requests") AT 3

-- expected: FULFILLED (day 20 of 21 calendar days that hold 15 working days)
#TRACE `s 805(1) the company must make the report available for inspection after the conclusion of the investigation` 21 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(1) makes the report available for inspection") AT 20

-- expected: DEONTIC BREACHED
#TRACE `s 805(1) the company must make the report available for inspection after the conclusion of the investigation` 21 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(1) makes the report available for inspection") AT 22

-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 805(5) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place at which the reports are kept` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 805(5) gives notice of the place at which the reports are kept available for inspection and of any change in that place") AT 2

-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 805(6) the company must notify the members who made the requests where the report is available` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(6) notifies the members who made the requests where the report is available for inspection") AT 3

-- expected: DEONTIC BREACHED
#TRACE `s 805(6) the company must notify the members who made the requests where the report is available` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(6) notifies the members who made the requests where the report is available for inspection") AT 4

-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 807(2) the company must provide the copy after the request is received` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 807(2) provides the person with a copy of the report or part of it") AT 14

-- expected: DEONTIC BREACHED
#TRACE `s 807(2) the company must provide the copy after the request is received` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 807(2) provides the person with a copy of the report or part of it") AT 15

-- expected: DEONTIC BREACHED (an exemption granted without consulting the Governor)
#TRACE `s 796(2) the Secretary of State must not grant the exemption unless the conditions are met` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Secretary of State` DOES (`Action of a party` OF `Secretary of State`, Company, "s 796(2) grants an exemption from the operation of section 793") AT 1

-- expected: FULFILLED (the conditions are met: nothing prohibited)
#TRACE `s 796(2) the Secretary of State must not grant the exemption unless the conditions are met` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Secretary of State` DOES (`Action of a party` OF `Secretary of State`, Company, "s 796(2) grants an exemption from the operation of section 793") AT 1

